      en: "Mount Alvand (Alvand Kuh) is a mountain in Hamadan Province, western Iran. At 3,580 m, it is the highest peak of the Alvand range. The mountain is composed of metamorphic rock, primarily granite. It is known for archaeological sites, including Sassanid-era rock reliefs. The region has a continental climate with cold winters and mild summers. Slopes are covered with oak and juniper. The mountain is a popular hiking destination with rich birdlife. Nearby are the historic cities of Hamadan and Ecbatana. The name derives from an Elamite word.",
